Problem Statement



Julia is building a text analysis tool and needs to verify if a given string is a palindrome, ignoring case sensitivity.



Help Julia by writing a program that takes a string as input and checks if it reads the same forwards and backward. Use java.lang.StringBuilder for string manipulation.

Input format :
The input consists of a string.

Output format :
The output prints the original string followed by either:



"is a palindrome" if it is a palindrome

"is not a palindrome" if it is not a palindrome



Refer to the sample output for formatting specifications.

Code constraints :
The given test cases fall under the following constraints:

Maximum length of the string: 50

The string contains spaces, lowercase and uppercase letters

The comparison is case-insensitive

Sample test cases :
    Input 1 :
        madam
    Output 1 :
        madam is a palindrome

          
    Input 2 :
        cat
    Output 2 :
        cat is not a palindrome
